# The repository is public, and the editor's password and GitHub token are the
# two things that must never land in it. They live in the Cloudflare Pages
# project (Settings → Environment variables) and nowhere else.
#
# These patterns are the belt to that braces: the file names Wrangler and every
# other tool reach for when you keep secrets locally, ignored before they can
# be committed by an absent-minded `git add -A`.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.env
.env.*
*.secret

# Wrangler's working directory, if you ever run it here.
.wrangler/

# The usual rubbish.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
